<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="viewer-match-day" data-rev="3">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/match-state.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure reducer from event, stats, and condition messages to the match state at a tick. Every message is released by the rendered tick, never by arrival, because the stream leads playback by up to 500 ticks.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ state</td><td>+200</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/feed.mjs, scoreboard.mjs, goal-moment.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Per-frame feed batcher with one fragment insert per frame; the 56-pixel header with crests, score bug, clock, and speed; the goal pulse, banner, and highlight inside 1.5 seconds, with reduced motion respected.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ panels</td><td>+400</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/lineups.mjs, stats.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Lineup rows from the hello roster, with a fatigue bar from the condition message and a state word beside every colour; the nine-row statistics grid read from the stats.* keys.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ panels</td><td>+300</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/components/panels.css</summary><div class="pl-card">Score bug, banner, feed, lineup, and statistics styles on the existing tokens; opacity and transform transitions only.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/ page</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/index.html, main.mjs, layout.css, tokens.css, pitch.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Panel markup replaces the empty regions; one flush per frame from the rendered tick; a read-only matchDay() hook; full time named apart from a dropped stream; parked markers hidden.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web/ page</td><td>+188 / -41</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> web/tests/match-state, feed, stats, lineups, pitch; helpers (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">Goal visible at its tick and not before; a 40-event burst inserted with none dropped; every statistics field equal; every fatigue band carries a word; parked markers hidden.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web/tests</td><td>+490</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol, docs/reference/protocol.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Protocol version 3. A roster on each hello team (starters in wire-slot order, then the bench); nine stats.* pairs on the stats message; a new condition message with 22 energy values.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/protocol and docs</td><td>+155 / -7</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">service</span> crates/engine-cli (stream_run, serve, record, bench)</summary><div class="pl-card">One hello_teams helper for three commands; stats and condition sent once per simulated second from the counters and rounding the match-stats record already uses; the simulation is created before the hello.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+94 / -54</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/stream/tests (common, fixture)</summary><div class="pl-card">Test hello and stats literals fill the new fields.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/stream tests</td><td>+16</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · Messages arrive ahead of playback</div><div class="callout-body">Showing an event, a statistic, or an energy value on arrival would run ahead of the pitch. Every message is released by the rendered tick, tested with a goal arriving 400 ticks early.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R6 · Version 3 refuses earlier recorded files</div><div class="callout-body">Replay refuses a recorded file whose header names another version. None is tracked; verification records a fresh one.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R9 · Periodic message volume</div><div class="callout-body">About 5,400 stats and 5,400 condition messages per full match. Energy is rounded to three decimals, and stream throughput and memory are re-measured against the 8.55 MB tripwire.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · Panels steal frame budget</div><div class="callout-body">One flush per frame, changed nodes only, statistics and energy per released message and never per tick.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · No reduced-motion emulation in the browser tool</div><div class="callout-body">A proxy attribute shares the media query's CSS block; the real query is checked when the operator turns off Windows animation effects.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R10 · The lineup editor changes the roster before kick-off</div><div class="callout-body">Roster entries carry the squad index, so the next viewer slice can re-order them under the same version.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R8 · A later event-contract redesign renames event kinds</div><div class="callout-body">The new modules keep every event-kind string in one table, and the feed batcher does not depend on the event count.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>3 prior revisions</summary><ul><li>rev 0 (2026-09-22): first plan, awaiting input on Q-1 (scope here, re-sequence, or proposed contract).</li><li>rev 1 (2026-09-23): auto-review re-grounded on the shipped producers; Q-1 narrowed to the wire shape with three options.</li><li>rev 2 (2026-09-23): drift review adds the event-contract redesign risk; Q-1 still open. Superseded when the product owner chose option A.</li></ul></details>
  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-revs { margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 28, modules = 7;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
